$NetBSD$

The bundled Makefile sets EMACS itself.  pkgsrc passes EMACS in MAKE_ENV, so
comment the assignment out and let that one through -- otherwise the package is
compiled by whatever "emacs" is first on PATH, not by the one it was built for.

--- Makefile.orig	Wed May 16 22:18:21 2001
+++ Makefile
@@ -20,7 +20,7 @@
 # Use whichever you like most
 #EMACS = xemacs
 #EMACS = /usr/local/bin/emacs
-EMACS = emacs
+#EMACS = emacs
 
 # If your operating system does not support file links (e.g. Windows),
 # change this to an ordinary copy command
